                    "The club wanted to explain the reused scenery in the programme. Tunde drafted a note describing the old productions and the decision to use approved materials again. The school archivist checked the dates and corrected one title. The club also credited the maintenance team and costume supervisor for their work.",
                    "They avoided claiming that every old item had been saved. The programme explained that some materials were unsuitable for reuse and had been handled through the school's normal process. The students thought honesty made the reuse project more meaningful, not less."
