                StoryPart(8, "Opening Night", listOf(
                    "The hall filled with families and students. The first scene used the blue panel as a river, then turned it into a library wall with a simple sign. The cast moved the lightweight props according to the rehearsed plan, while the stage supervisor checked the approved frames before the audience entered.",
                    "The performance received warm applause. Afterward, several younger students asked how the club had made the set work with so few materials. Tunde showed them the design sketches and explained how the team had planned around safety and reuse instead of building everything from scratch."
                )),
                StoryPart(9, "A Second Use", listOf(
                    "The school asked whether the flexible set could be adapted for a reading event. The drama club agreed to lend the approved panels after the stage supervisor checked the new layout. The archivist added photographs of the production to the school collection, while the costume supervisor updated the borrowing record.",
                    "The club wrote a short guide for the next drama team. It included the inventory process, the approved materials list, and the contact details for staff who could authorise changes. They made clear that future students should repeat the inspection rather than assume the scenery would remain safe forever."
