                StoryPart(10, "The Stage That Stayed", listOf(
                    "At the end of term, the old storage area was organised, with unsafe items separated for proper disposal and reusable pieces labelled. The drama club had created a production without a large construction budget, but its best achievement was the process it left behind: inventory, permission, inspection, planning, and credit.",
                    "Tunde looked at the blue panel leaning neatly in the approved storage rack. It had been a river, a wall, and a doorway, but it had never needed to become something expensive. The secondhand stage had shown the school that imagination could make good use of what already existed."
